WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.090
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:03.480
- Science can make a big difference,

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:06.240
anywhere from just a simple reaction

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.070
to a big experiment.

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:09.502
If you just find the right application,

00:00:09.502 --> 00:00:11.780
science can save the world.

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:16.220
My name is Gitanjali Rao,
and I'm 12 years old.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:17.370
I'm a scientist.

00:00:24.735 --> 00:00:26.910
I invented a device called Tethys

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.620
that detects leads in water faster

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.540
than any other current
techniques out there today.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:34.770
I was appalled by the number of people

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.555
affected by lead in water

00:00:36.555 --> 00:00:39.150
during the Flint water crisis.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:40.694
I wanted to do something to change this

00:00:40.694 --> 00:00:42.002
for the residents of Flint

00:00:42.002 --> 00:00:44.640
and places like Flint all over the world.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:49.070
My device includes a core device

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:50.474
and a disposable cartridge

00:00:50.474 --> 00:00:52.692
with the carbon in a tube sensor.

00:00:52.692 --> 00:00:55.710
You dip this disposable
cartridge into the water

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:56.630
you wanna test.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:59.171
You pull out your phone, open
up the Tethis application,

00:00:59.171 --> 00:01:03.020
and connect over Bluetooth
to get the results

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:05.366
of safe, slightly
contaminated, or critical

00:01:05.366 --> 00:01:07.360
of lead levels in your water.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:12.430
My advice to other kids

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:16.150
who wanna save the world
is do not be afraid to try.

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:18.490
I failed like four or five times,

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:20.100
but I got back into the lab,

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.599
did it again, and then it
was like the a-ha moment

00:01:22.599 --> 00:01:24.939
when everything kind of
started coming together

00:01:24.939 --> 00:01:27.310
and, you know, the device is born.

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:29.980
I think that science allows me

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:31.440
to look at different approaches

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.714
to solve real-world
problems out there today.

00:01:33.714 --> 00:01:36.790
It's important to take
other people's problems

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:40.524
and make something to help them with it,

00:01:40.524 --> 00:01:43.470
mainly because we're all one big community,

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.420
and it's our duty to help other people.

